# Band boundaries: Unicode CLDR 47 Day Period Rules, locale el
# (https://www.unicode.org/cldr/charts/47/supplemental/day_periods.html),
# transcribed in chronologia/dayparts.py as afternoon [12:00, 17:00) (CLDR
# afternoon1+afternoon2 collapsed into chronologia's four-band model).
# Surface: απόγευμα (apógevma), the neuter noun for "afternoon"; used bare
# as an adverb ("in the afternoon") and after the article ("το απόγευμα").
# Source: Wiktionary, "απόγευμα" (noun, gender "n"), which glosses "το
# απόγευμα" as its own worked example.
# https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/απόγευμα
# Gender confirms the neuter accusative article "το" (Wiktionary, "το",
# neuter nominative/accusative singular of "ο":
# https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/το).
απόγευμα
